# Local caches
.cache/
.turbo/
# ANCHORED with a leading slash, and it must stay that way. A bare `lib/` matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, so it silently swallowed `apps/web/src/lib/` — the
# entire tool layer of the chat surface — while `git status` stayed clean and the tests
# passed locally because the files were right there. `src/lib/` is a standard source
# layout, and `cache/` can name a source module just as easily; both of these are real
# directories at the repo ROOT and that is the only place they should be ignored.
# Unanchored patterns are fine for `dist/`, `build/`, `out/` and `coverage/` above, whose
# names mean build output wherever they appear.
/lib/
contracts/out/
/cache/

# Sandbox litter. `HOME` is redirected to the skill's own directory so a job cannot read
# the seller's home by relative path (packages/runner/src/exec.ts), which means anything a
# job runs writes its dotfiles and caches THERE. Regenerable, and it must never be
# committed alongside a skill.
skills/*/Library/
skills/*/.cache/
skills/*/.bun/
skills/*/.npm/
skills/*/.config/

# Generated video assets. The SOURCES are committed — docs/narration/*.txt is the script and
# scripts/narrate.sh regenerates every clip from it — so these are derived bytes, and the
# same reasoning that keeps a second copy of a money field out of this codebase keeps
# regenerable media out of its history.
design/
